  "introduction": {
    "text": "The Basilica di Santa Maria sopra Minerva in Rome is a minor basilica and the only surviving example of original Gothic church architecture in the city. Its layered history—from a Roman temple to a Dominican centre—makes it a key monument of religious, artistic, and architectural heritage.",
    "sourceIds": [
      "wikipedia"
    ]
  },
